arily large counterexamples with h(G)<26m/75+2/3<m/2<=chi_f(G)<=chi(G), and consequently disproves Hadwiger. The configured not_hadwiger_conjecture is precisely that final non-universality consequence. The formal existence theorem also contains the integer chromatic bounds, but no claim about fractional chromatic number is attributed to it here.","fingerprint":"sha256:dc2fd89aa33b842d84c0d1ace2dfdad8102e09f23ea391d937b41e3c8e063008","limitations":"This is an agent source reading, not a proof replay or independently reviewed equivalence.","relation":"formal-is-consequence","row_id":"A-counterexample-to-Hadwigers-conjecture-September-23-2026#cor:hadwiger","statement_sha256":"sha256:93174cf52c34e0de3c5cfc41ead65f014a1ff058aa19da7de72ec0fec55a878f"}]},"pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","provenance":{"identity_assurance":"named local attestation; identity not independently authenticated","kind":"agent-drafted-unreviewed"},"references":["https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/lean/ComparatorChallenges/HadwigerCounterexample.lean","https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/A-counterexample-to-Hadwigers-conjecture-September-23-2026/build/sections/01-introduction.tex#L20","https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/A-counterexample-to-Hadwigers-conjecture-September-23-2026/build/sections/01-introduction.tex#L48"],"release_id":"openai-math","review_state":"unreviewed","row_id":"challenge:HadwigerCounterexample","schema":"statement-map-contribution/1"}],"detail":{"path":"lean/272dbf47d91e17e5f6224609.json","pointer":""},"formal_statement":{"detail":{"path":"lean/272dbf47d91e17e5f6224609.json","pointer":"/reader/formal_statement"},"full_source":{"path":"lean/272dbf47d91e17e5f6224609.json","pointer":"/reader/formal_statement"},"kind":"declaration-signatures","method":"configured-challenge-declaration-signatures","name_resolution":"source-te